sn1.20:28.1 starts: In all the world,
sn1.20:28.2 starts: you should do no evil
sn1.20:28.3 starts: Having abandoned sensuality
sn1.20:28.4 starts: don’t consort
sn1.36:5.1 starts: They’re devoted to heedlessness
sn1.36:5.2 starts: —dullards, fools—
sn1.36:5.3 starts: while one who is wise
sn1.36:5.4 starts: as his highest wealth.
sn1.38:9.1 starts: “Five-Veda Brahmans,
sn1.38:9.2 starts: living austerely
sn1.38:9.3 starts: Their minds
sn1.38:9.4 starts: Lowly by nature,
sn1.42:3.1 starts: And the one who gives a residence
sn1.42:3.2 starts: is the one who’s a giver of
sn1.42:3.3 starts: But the one who teaches the Dhamma
sn1.42:3.4 starts: is a giver of
sn1.71:3.1 starts: The Buddha:
sn1.71:3.2 starts: Having killed anger
sn1.71:3.3 starts: The noble ones praise
sn1.71:3.4 starts: the slaying of anger
sn1.71:3.5 starts: —with its honeyed crest
sn1.71:3.6 starts: for having killed it
